# model_table -- the single per-model definition file: every per-model *fact*
# (plus deliberate per-model policy overrides) lives here once; hardware bring-up
# comes from each camera's stock lower_half_init.sh (gen-lower-half.sh).
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated); a row here is a claim about real hardware.
#   model        model_suffix token: what /backup/init.sh sets and -m carries
#   sensor       MIPI driver basename; used only when one row names it (gc2053 is shared)
#   ring_offset  fshare ring control-header size (bytes); 0 = autodetect
#   ring_header  per-frame header bytes before payload; 0 = autodetect
#   high_w/h     HIGH-channel (video1) geometry the STOCK rmm encoder streams
#                (SPS-verified from rmm; may be an ISP upscale of the sensor)
#   ptz          yes/no -- real motorized pan/tilt base
#   high_bitrate HIGH-channel bitrate to pin (bps); 0 = follow the controller's
#                target (a deliberate per-model policy override, e.g. y623's weak
#                2.4 GHz link). The encoder target and both declared bitrates
#                (Go client + bridge) are pinned together.
#   mediad_w/h   HIGH geometry the clean-room mediad streams; absent = same as
#                high_w/h. The bridge/client pick this row whenever the camera is
#                on the mediad path (yi-protect.cfg IS_MEDIAD=yes + installed), so the
#                DECLARED geometry always matches the ACTIVE encoder. h51ga is the
#                case that differs: rmm upscales to 2K, mediad streams native 1080p.
#   h265         yes/no -- this model's encoder produces valid H.265 (super
#                encoding), so the client advertises it to the controller. Only
#                y623 is validated; every other model advertises H.264 only (a
#                broken H.265 is what shows as a green stream).
#
# A row here means we own the hardware and can bring it up. No row = conservative
# default (368/28, 2304x1296, no PTZ) + warning, never a silent guess.
y623     gc3003  368  28  2304  1296  no   2800000  2304  1296  yes
h51ga    gc2053  368  28  2304  1296  yes  0        1920  1080  no
h52ga    gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  yes  0        1920  1080  no
r35gb    gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  yes  0        1920  1080  no
y291ga   gc2053  368  28  1920  1080  no   0        1920  1080  no
